course: dictionary
lesson: 8618
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The best way to choose the right one is to look at the words around it. «Screw» is a good example: it can be a small metal pin, or a verb that means to twist something.
explain: «Suck a slice of lemon and your whole face screws up.» Here screws up does not mean fixing anything with a screwdriver. Your face squeezes into a tight, scrunched shape, so screw up means squeeze or crumple. Always ask: what would fit in this sentence?
explain: Phrases can change the meaning too. «I screwed up my spelling test» means I made a mistake. Nobody is talking about metal pins there. «Has a screw loose» is a joke that means a bit mad or acting strangely.
fact: A screw is a small pointed metal pin with a spiral ridge, turned with a screwdriver to hold things together.
fact: «Screw» can be a noun (a screw) or a verb (to screw something on, as in «screw on the lid»).
fact: «Screw up» can mean to squeeze or crumple, as in «screw up the paper».
fact: In everyday talk, «screw up» can also mean to make a mistake or a mess.
fact: A screw is one of the simple machines, like a twisted ramp, and it can move a valve up and down in a tap.
exercise: «The lid is screwed tightly onto the jar.» What does screwed mean here? | Broken into pieces | Squeezed into a ball | *Fixed by turning, like a screw | Made a mistake
exercise: «Suck a slice of lemon and your whole face screws up.» What does screws up mean? | Fixes with a screwdriver | Smiles widely | *Squeezes into a tight, scrunched shape | Grows bigger
exercise: «I screwed up my spelling test.» What does screwed up mean? | Fixed it with a screwdriver | *Made a mistake | Won a prize | Turned round and round
test: Why do some taps need many turns to open fully? | *Because a screw thread moves a valve up and down a little | Because the water is cold | Because the handle is painted red | Because taps are always broken
test: Which sentence uses screw as a noun? | The paper was screwed up into a ball. | *The shelf needs four new screws. | Please screw the lid on tightly.
exam: A friend says, «You've got a screw loose!» What does this joke mean? | *They think you are a bit mad or acting strangely | They think you are very tall | They think you should fix the chair | They think you need new glasses
